# The sdist is the complete project, not just the importable part.
#
# README.md links to docs/ and examples/ with relative paths, and setuptools
# does not ship either by default -- so without this the sdist arrives with
# its own front page pointing at files that are not there. The doc-drift
# tests read those same files, so an sdist missing them cannot run its own
# suite either.
include LICENSE
include NOTICE
include CHANGELOG.md
include RELEASING.md
include SECURITY.md
recursive-include docs *.md
recursive-include examples *.md *.json *.sh *.py *.txt
recursive-include tools *.py

# Run stores are outputs, not source, and are no longer tracked -- but they
# still exist on disk after anyone runs the examples, and MANIFEST.in reads
# the FILESYSTEM rather than git. Without a prune per store the sdist sweeps
# them back in, and sweeps them in BROKEN: `attempts.jsonl` and `*.bin` match
# none of the include patterns above, so the shipped run would carry an
# integrity.json whose subjects are missing and could not pass `hwb verify`.
#
# One line per store directory. A test asserts this list covers every store
# present under examples/, because a new example is exactly when this is
# forgotten.
prune examples/runs
prune examples/flaky/runs
prune examples/flaky/sweeps
prune examples/flaky/catches
prune examples/flaky/efficacy
prune examples/flaky/steadies
prune examples/attaching/runs
prune examples/attaching/steadies
prune examples/effect-boundary/runs
prune examples/effect-boundary/effects
prune examples/interrupts
prune examples/flaky/interrupts
prune examples/attaching/interrupts
prune examples/effect-boundary/interrupts
